<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso II of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1157">1157</a>–1196</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Alfonso the Chaste</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso II was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer IV of Barcelona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petronilla-of-aragon">Petronila of Aragon</a>. He became Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in 1162 and King of Aragon in 1164, the first ruler to hold both by inheritance, uniting them in what became the Crown of Aragon. He secured Provence for his family, extended Aragon south against the Muslims, founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teruel">Teruel</a> and was a patron of troubadour poetry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Alfonso II of Aragon" width="202" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: derivative work: Escarlati (talk) Liber_feudorum_maior.jpg: unknow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfonso_II_de_Arag%C3%B3n_from_Liber_feudorum_maior.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
